        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0551" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg457"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker, chargé, to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Managua, Nicaragua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-16"><hi rendition="#italic">October 16, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Nov. 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 715.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith copies of telegrams
                    addressed to and sent from this legation upon the change in the diplomatic
                    relations between the United States and the Governments of Nicaragua and
                    Salvador.</p>
                <p>The late minister of foreign relations in Salvador, Señor J. Castellanos, states
                    very clearly that the Diet assumes the functions of the offices of foreign
                    relations of the three Republics.</p>
                <p>I had the honor to send you a copy of the circular to which his excellency refers
                    in my No. 714 of October 14.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John F. Baker</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d360-a1.xml" xpointer="d360-a1"/>
